+# Bun migration
+
+Use Bun 1.4.4 or newer. This migration was verified with Bun 1.4.4 on macOS
+ARM64; the original baseline used Deno 2.9.7.
+
+```sh
+bun install --frozen-lockfile
+bun run typecheck
+bun run check
+bun run test
+bun run run new /tmp/example.txt 'héllo 🌎'
+bun run run read /tmp/example.txt
+```
+
+The `run` and `check` entry points replace the original Deno tasks. `typecheck`
+uses Bun's native checker with strict TypeScript settings and covers all source
+files, including `src/child.ts`, and the regression tests. `check` invokes the
+same checker. No serve or build tasks existed. Formatting and linting were not
+added or changed.
+
+There were no original external dependencies to preserve. The only new direct
+dependency is the development declaration package `@types/bun`, pinned to 1.4.4;
+its transitive declarations are recorded in the generated `bun.lock`. No runtime
+packages or trusted installation scripts are required. `deno.json` was removed.
+
+## Preserved behavior
+
+- `new` uses exclusive creation (`wx`) and never overwrites an existing file.
+- `replace` creates absent files and truncates existing content. Omitted text
+  remains an empty string. Reads and writes use UTF-8.
+- `missing` recognizes nonexistent paths by `ENOENT`, and propagates other
+  filesystem errors. Runtime-specific error names, messages, and stack traces
+  differ; failures still exit unsuccessfully.
+- `list` returns sorted regular filenames and excludes directories and symlinks.
+- `child` executes the adjacent TypeScript child with the current Bun executable,
+  converts its file URL to a filesystem path, ignores stdin, and drains both
+  output pipes concurrently. It returns JSON containing exit code 7 and the
+  complete stdout/stderr strings. The parent exits successfully as before.
+- `bunfig.toml` disables automatic dotenv loading, matching the original runtime.
+
+## Security and operational differences
+
+Bun has no equivalent to Deno's permission sandbox. The original launcher granted
+filesystem reads, writes, and subprocess execution, but withheld other permissions
+such as network and environment access. Bun runs with the user's normal OS
+privileges, including those additional capabilities. Use an OS sandbox or
+container if that boundary is required for untrusted execution. No permissions,
+services, or global tools were changed by this migration.
+
+## Verification
+
+The original strict Deno check and 12 filesystem/process baseline checks passed.
+There were no original tests or skips. Six Bun regression tests (18 assertions,
+zero failures/skips) now cover exclusive creation, Unicode reads, truncation,
+creation, omitted text, missing-file classification, directory errors, sorted
+listing, symlinks, unknown operations, and the large subprocess streams
+(120,001 bytes per stream) and exit status.
+
+A fresh disposable copy installed successfully using `bun install
+--frozen-lockfile --offline`, with no copied `node_modules`, using the downloaded
+package cache. Both strict check commands and the tests passed with Deno absent
+from PATH. Additional probes verified package-script argument forwarding with
+spaces and Unicode, that dotenv stays disabled through the outer script runner
+and inner runtime, and that an intentional type error in `src/child.ts` causes
+`typecheck` to fail. The probes and intentional error were confined to the
+disposable copy and removed afterward.
+
+Validation was local on macOS; other operating systems and hosted environments
+were not tested. There is no deployment or hosted CI configuration in this
+project.
